          ))
        }
      </ol>
      <div class="engineering-note firmware-example" aria-labelledby="scan-example-title">
        <p class="small-label">FIRMWARE / C++17</p>
        <h3 id="scan-example-title">Find the probe instead of losing the reading.</h3>
        <p>
          When a probe stops answering, the driver asks once more, then sweeps the bus read-only. A unit that answers
          the temperature/moisture registers and a valid pH register is the THP probe; one without pH is the TH probe.
        </p>
        <p class="note">soil_probes.cpp · SoilProbes::scan</p>
        <details class="code-toggle">
          <summary>Show the C++ excerpt</summary>
          <Code
            code={scanExample}
            lang="cpp"
            themes={{ light: 'github-light', dark: 'github-dark' }}
            tabindex="0"
            aria-labelledby="scan-example-title"
            data-firmware-code="true"
          />
        </details>
        <p class="note">
          A new address is used only if it does not belong to the other probe, and it is saved for the next start.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="engineering-note">
        <p class="small-label">BEFORE THE FIRST FIELD READING</p>
        <h3>A response is evidence. Accuracy needs more.</h3>
        <p>
          On 17 November, separate single-query tests returned valid responses with one probe in water, dry soil and the
          same soil after wetting. The moisture register changed after wetting. Temperature and moisture units follow
          the seller manual; these checks do not establish calibration, accuracy or reliable long-term operation.
        </p>
        <p>
          On 21 November, the production firmware ran on the 12 V adapter with both probes reporting good readings in
          air and uploads acknowledged by the cloud. Readings in air are not soil measurements. Cable routing,
          protection, sealed joints and suitability for burial are checked during installation.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="note">
        Hardware snapshot: 21 November 2026 · Two probes uploading from the bench · OTA updates working · Field
        installation in progress.
      </p>
